---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import jsonLd from '../data/index-jsonld';
import { APP_LOGIN_URL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lucid Cashflow · Cashflow, sorted."
  description="Lucid connects to Xero, forecasts your cash 13 weeks ahead, and tells you each day whether you need to do anything, and what. Free to start."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid">
<div class="hero-copy">
<span class="eyebrow">For UK businesses on Xero</span>
<h1>Cashflow, sorted<span class="dot">.</span></h1>
<p class="lede">Lucid understands, anticipates and manages your cashflow so you can focus on building the business.</p>
<div class="actions" id="start"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={APP_LOGIN_URL}>Build your forecast free</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/demo/">See a 60-second demo</a></div>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:.95rem">Read-only connection to Xero · Free to start · Built by former bank credit-risk specialists</p>
</div>
<div class="phone" aria-label="Example of the Lucid daily verdict">
<div class="phone-top"><span>Today · Mon 2 Nov</span><span class="mono">Synced 08:02</span></div>
<div class="verdict good"><span class="tag">● Nothing to do today</span>
<span class="say">You’re covered to 14 January.</span>
<span class="why">Payroll on 27 November is safe. Lowest point: <span class="mono">£18,400</span> in week 9.</span></div>
<div><div class="bars" aria-hidden="true"><span style="height:72%"></span><span style="height:80%"></span><span style="height:66%"></span><span style="height:58%"></span><span style="height:70%"></span><span style="height:62%"></span><span style="height:49%"></span><span style="height:41%"></span><span class="low" style="height:24%"></span><span style="height:38%"></span><span style="height:52%"></span><span style="height:61%"></span><span style="height:68%"></span></div>
<div class="bars-legend"><span>Wk 1</span><span>13-week cash</span><span>Wk 13</span></div></div>
<div class="verdict warn"><span class="tag">● Worth a look · week 9</span><span class="why">VAT of <span class="mono">£12,600</span> lands as two customers pay late, taking you below your <span class="mono">£20,000</span> buffer. Cheapest ways to protect it:</span>
<div class="ways"><div class="way"><b>Chase 2 overdue invoices</b><span class="mono">£0</span></div><div class="way"><b>Move a supplier run by 1 week</b><span class="mono">£0</span></div><div class="way"><b>Short-term facility</b><span class="mono">from panel</span></div></div></div>
<p class="example">Example business. Figures are illustrative.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="proof-section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="proof">
<div><b>13 weeks</b><span>of cash ahead, week by week</span></div>
<div><b>One verdict</b><span>every morning: fine, or act now</span></div>
<div><b>Cheapest first</b><span>free fixes before any funding</span></div>
<div><b>Read-only</b><span>we never change your books</span></div>
</div></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">How it works</span><h2>Time is the fix.</h2>
<p class="lede">Most cash problems are visible weeks before they hurt. Lucid makes sure you see them while you still have options.</p></div>
<div class="grid-3">
<div class="card"><span class="step-num">01 · See it</span><h3>Your cash, 13 weeks ahead</h3><p>Connect Xero and answer five plain questions about your business. Lucid builds a week-by-week forecast in minutes, with payroll, VAT and PAYE on their real dates.</p></div>
<div class="card"><span class="step-num">02 · Spot it</span><h3>A verdict every morning</h3><p>Most days the answer is “nothing to do, you’re fine”. When something material changes, like a big customer paying late, Lucid tells you what, when and how much.</p></div>
<div class="card"><span class="step-num">03 · Fix it</span><h3>Ways through, cheapest first</h3><p>Move a payment. Chase the right invoices. Only then, if it’s needed, an orderly application to an impartial panel of lenders, with the pack already built.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">What owners use Lucid for</span><h2>The cash questions that keep you up at 2am</h2></div>
<div class="grid-2">
<div class="card"><h3>“Can I make payroll?”</h3><p>The Payroll Safety Light shows whether your next payroll, and the PAYE and pension that follow, are covered. If not, Lucid shows how to close the gap.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>“Where did that VAT bill come from?”</h3><p>VAT, PAYE and Corporation Tax sit in your forecast on their real dates, weeks ahead, so they stop being surprises.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>“A big customer is paying late.”</h3><p>Lucid learns how each customer really pays and shows the knock-on effect, then tells you which invoices to chase first.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>“Can we afford to grow?”</h3><p>Ask “what if we hire two people in March?” or “what if we take the bigger order?” and see the next 13 weeks change before you commit.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">Why Lucid</span><h2>Your accounts tell you what happened. Lucid tells you what’s coming.</h2></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th style="width:28%"></th><th>Accounting software on its own</th><th>With Lucid</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>What you see</td><td>What has been invoiced, paid and reconciled</td><td>Your cash week by week for the next 13 weeks, and beyond</td></tr>
<tr><td>Customer payments</td><td>Due dates on invoices</td><td>When each customer actually tends to pay</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tax and payroll</td><td>Entered when they happen</td><td>VAT, PAYE and Corporation Tax placed on their real due dates in advance</td></tr>
<tr><td>What it tells you to do</td><td>Nothing; you interpret the reports</td><td>A plain verdict and ranked options, with the cost of each</td></tr>
<tr><td>If you need funding</td><td>You start from scratch, usually in a hurry</td><td>A lender-ready pack and weeks of runway left to apply calmly</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
</div></section>

<section class="statement"><div class="wrap narrow" style="display:grid;gap:18px">
<span class="eyebrow">An honest word about funding</span>
<h2>We can’t guarantee funding. We can give you the best chance.</h2>
<p>We’ve spent our careers on the lender’s side of the table, building the credit models UK banks use. The pattern never changes: a business that applies early, calmly, with a forecast and no missed payments, gets a better hearing than one that applies the week payroll is due. Lucid is built to make you the first kind.</p>
<p><a href="/about/" style="color:inherit">Read why we built Lucid →</a></p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:start">
<div class="section-head" style="margin:0"><span class="eyebrow">Questions</span><h2>What owners ask first</h2><p class="lede">Can’t see your question? Email hello@lucidcashflow.co.uk and a founder will reply.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><details><summary>Does Lucid work with Xero?</summary><p>Yes. You connect Xero in a couple of clicks with read-only access. Lucid reads your invoices, bills, bank transactions and payroll, and never changes your books or moves money. QuickBooks and Sage are on the roadmap.</p></details><details><summary>How is this different from the forecast in Xero?</summary><p>Xero shows a projection of your bank balance. Lucid builds a 13-week forecast from how your customers actually pay, adds tax and payroll on their real dates, then tells you each day whether you need to act, and what the cheapest fix is.</p></details><details><summary>Is Lucid trying to sell me a loan?</summary><p>No. Most days Lucid tells you there is nothing to do. When a squeeze is coming, it shows the free fixes first. Funding only appears when it is genuinely the right answer, and only goes to a lender if you say yes.</p></details><details><summary>Who builds the numbers, a person or AI?</summary><p>Lucid’s AI writes the forecast as code, and the code calculates every figure from your ledger. That makes the numbers reproducible and checkable. The AI explains the results; it never makes up a figure.</p></details><details><summary>What size of business is Lucid for?</summary><p>Founder-led UK limited companies, typically with 10 to 200 staff, using Xero and without a full-time finance director.</p></details><details><summary>Will Lucid replace my accountant?</summary><p>No. Your accountant keeps your books right and your tax filed. Lucid looks forward, week by week, and you can share your forecast with your accountant.</p></details></div>
</div></section>

<section class="cta-band" id="early"><div class="wrap">
<div style="display:grid;gap:10px"><h2>Build your forecast free.</h2><p class="muted">Early access is opening now for UK limited companies on Xero.</p></div>
<div style="display:grid;gap:10px">
<form class="signup" aria-label="Early access"><label for="email-get" class="sr" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px">Work email</label>
<input id="email-get" type="email" required placeholder="you@yourbusiness.co.uk" autocomplete="email">
<button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Get early access</button></form>
<p class="form-done" hidden>Thanks. You’re on the list, and we’ll be in touch soon.</p>
<p class="form-note">We’re opening Lucid to businesses in small groups. Leave your email and we’ll send your invite.</p></div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
